Sval: RFPTargets.inc includes Sval's targets, and nsRFPService.h Sval's helpers

Sval's RFPTargets live in SvalRFPTargets.inc and the helpers that spoof them in
SvalRFPService.h and .cpp, files Sval adds, so each fp-* patch changes only the
call sites that ask them. A target added to Mozilla's list, or a reordered
series, then conflicts with no fp patch. RFPTargets.inc includes the Sval list
where Mozilla's targets end, and extract_rfp_targets.py reads the include in
place as the preprocessor does, so RFPTargetConstants.sys.mjs lists every
target in the same order. nsRFPService.h includes SvalRFPService.h after its
own declarations, which the helpers use, so every file that sees
nsRFPService sees them.

An RFPTarget is an enumerator of the list RFPTargets.inc defines, and the
build generates the JS constants from that file's text, so no chrome API can
add one.

